Ladybird now resolves a replaced grid item’s percentage height against
its grid area while the columns are sized, and doesn’t compress the
item’s automatic minimum height to zero. Run in Chrome 157.0.8103.79,
Firefox 151.0, and Playwright’s WebKit 26.5, all three engines
grow the auto row to 450px.

In Blink, GridLayoutAlgorithm::CreateConstraintSpaceForMeasure()
resolves percentages against the tracks
that the item spans, and CalculateIntrinsicMinimumContribution()
measures the block contribution uncompressed: The compression in
ComputeMinAndMaxContentContributionForReplaced() tests only the width.
WebKit’s GridTrackSizingAlgorithm treats the grid area as indefinite in
the first column pass, in shouldTreatGridAreaBlockSizeAsIndefinite(),
and its minContributionForGridItem() measures the item’s block
size uncompressed. Gecko’s GridReflowInput::PercentageBasisFor()
uses the item’s tracks, and nsLayoutUtils::AddIntrinsicSizeOffset()
compresses only in the inline axis.
